Sure! I’ll outline exactly what you need to do so you can add a dark‑mode toggle **without touching the header** and also fix the “Save” button problem on mobile.

---

## 1️⃣ Add a Theme Context (if you don’t already have it)

Create `src/contexts/ThemeContext.jsx`:

```jsx
import React, { createContext, useState, useEffect } from 'react';

export const ThemeContext = createContext();

export const ThemeProvider = ({ children }) => {
  // Store user choice in localStorage so it persists
  const stored = localStorage.getItem('theme');
  const [theme, setTheme] = useState(stored || 'light');

  const toggleTheme = () => {
    const newTheme = theme === 'light' ? 'dark' : 'light';
    setTheme(newTheme);
    localStorage.setItem('theme', newTheme);
  };

  // Apply the theme class to the <html> element for global CSS hooks
  useEffect(() => {
    document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', theme);
  }, [theme]);

  return (
    <ThemeContext.Provider value={{ theme, toggleTheme }}>
      {children}
    </ThemeContext.Provider>
  );
};
```

Wrap your whole app in this provider (`index.jsx` or `App.jsx`):

```jsx
import { ThemeProvider } from './contexts/ThemeContext';

ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById('root')).render(
  <BrowserRouter>
    <ThemeProvider>
      <App />
    </ThemeProvider>
  </BrowserRouter>
);
```

